KZ3 patch 2075 (RSX pass 70): texture cache recycling, the RE notes "Pass 70".
KZ3's SPU jobs write per-object 8x8 W16Z16Y16X16_FLOAT parameter blocks into a ring in main memory
(1:0x0005C180-0x00C8F700 on K4, ~25,000 block slots), so each frame binds a few hundred blocks at offsets the texture
cache does not hold: on K4 they are 118,698 of the 125,184 new cache entries in 49 s (coord-fullclk-k4,
[perf-newtex-shape]). Past 8,192 entries every such miss scanned all entries for the smallest use serial, created a
512-byte committed resource and retired the victim's. Now (LD_TEX_RECYCLE, default on; =0 the old path) the victim
comes from an exact LRU list (libs/video/rsx_tex_lru.h, same order as the serials, O(1)) and the victim's resource is
offered to the decode as patch 2035's in-place target (reused when the description matches). [tex-hash] gains
evict=N recycle=N entries=N. Host test tools/smoke/test_tex_lru.sh.

